<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uberto Pallavicino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1197–<a href="/years/1269">1269</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uberto Pallavicino was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> nobleman and leader of the Ghibelline party, a supporter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>. From the 1250s he was lord of Cremona, Piacenza and other cities, and briefly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. His power collapsed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>'s victory in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1266, and he died in his castles.</p></div>
